<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaime Roldós Aguilera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaime Roldós Aguilera was a lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> who became the first president of Ecuador's restored democracy in 1979, after nearly a decade of military rule. His government promoted human rights in the region and faced a border war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in 1981. He died with his wife and others in an air crash in Loja province in May 1981.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaime-roldos-aguilera.jpg" alt="Jaime Roldós Aguilera" width="258" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Serrano · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaime_Rold%C3%B3s_Aguilera_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
